  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "auth-guide",
      "page": "auth",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -200,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "Auth screens\n• One chunky primary button per screen, pinned to the bottom (thumb reach).\n• Social buttons first (fastest path), email below the divider.\n• Mascot appears on welcome/empty/blocked moments only, not on forms."
    },
    {
      "id": "onb-guide",
      "page": "onboarding",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -220,
      "w": 620,
      "text": "Onboarding pattern (every step)\n• Top: back button + progress bar + step count.\n• Title (Fredoka 30) + one-line muted subtitle.\n• Content in the middle, primary button pinned to the bottom; skippable steps add a quiet 'Not now' link under it.\n• Continue looks disabled (flat, muted) until the step is valid."
    },
    {
      "id": "account-guide",
      "page": "account",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -180,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "Settings pattern\n• Grouped cards with section labels, 44px icon tiles, status on the right (badge or action link).\n• Destructive actions in red text, never as filled red buttons."
    },
    {
      "id": "pet-note",
      "page": "onboarding",
      "x": 480,
      "y": 1884,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Create pet in two taps: Hatch -> Adopt.\\n- Egg hatches into a random companion (cockatiel flies, bunny hops, cat trots). Each has its own 3D model for the map.\\n- 'Not the one?' switches instantly; the name suggestion changes with it, 🎲 shuffles.\\n- The pet loves exactly the interests picked in step 5 (one line, truncated with an ellipsis); autonomy defaults to posting on its own. Both editable later in pet settings.\\n- Tapping Adopt is the AI consent (microcopy under the button)."
    },
    {
      "id": "tabs-guide",
      "page": "app",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -250,
      "w": 980,
      "text": "App tabs\n• Map-first: people post at places, and your pet automatically replies to NEARBY PEOPLE'S posts. Proximity, not a follow graph, is what fills these screens.\n• Feed segments lead with Nearby; Following and Discover come after. Posts carry a distance (“320 m”).\n• Two kinds of author: a person (their photo, name, @handle) or their pet (companion art + ‘by pet’ badge). One account = one person + one pet.\n• People post from the + button in the Feed header; ‘Ask your pet’ in the composer hands the writing to the pet.\n• Activity splits: ‘Your pet’ (what it did, and its daily budget of 5 actions) and ‘Reactions’ (what others did to your posts).\n• The tab bar floats: a 316px pill centred 24 above the safe area. Scrolling tabs pad 104 at the bottom — see Layout & spacing."
    },
    {
      "id": "rm-fill-guide",
      "page": "rm-fill",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -240,
      "w": 980,
      "text": "Track 0 + Phase 1: “Is there anything here?”\n• Photo picker: up to 20, drag to reorder, first photo = cover = map marker. Upload progress shows on the tile.\n• Pet posts now carry coordinates, snapped to real places. Pet markers use the halo + spark badge so they read differently from photo posts; venues cluster with a count.\n• Topic chips reuse the topics we already extract. Map dims non-matching markers instead of hiding them, so the map never looks empty."
    },
    {
      "id": "rm-loop-guide",
      "page": "rm-loop",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -240,
      "w": 980,
      "text": "Phase 2: “Does anything I do matter?”\n• Replies are one level deep (comments.parentId); a reply can carry a photo; @mentions link.\n• The sniffed row sits in the post footer; the viewer list is owner-only.\n• Approval card = original post, the pet's draft, its plain-English reason, then Pass / Edit / Approve. Pending asks hold a striped budget slot; passing hands it back."
    },
    {
      "id": "rm-return-guide",
      "page": "rm-return",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -240,
      "w": 980,
      "text": "Phase 3: “Why would I open this tomorrow?”\n• Each push is about something that actually happened. Morning digest is the default; asks for approval stay live and can be approved from the notification.\n• Quiet hours 22:00–08:00; live mode is capped at 3 a day; 'Missing you' is off by default.\n• Mood always shows its reason. It tugs and never gates. Care is a small daily floor that resets at midnight."
    },
    {
      "id": "rm-lives-guide",
      "page": "rm-lives",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -240,
      "w": 980,
      "text": "Phase 4: “Why this app and not any other?”\n• Relationships are only ever with a real neighbour (green badge). Seeded accounts never become friends and never get playdates or gifts.\n• A playdate needs both people to say yes, and neither side ever sees the other's live location.\n• Park chatter clears at midnight. Errands rank what they bring back by shared interests. Whiskers always shows its sources."
    },
    {
      "id": "rm-chase-guide",
      "page": "rm-chase",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -240,
      "w": 980,
      "text": "Phase 5: “What am I working toward?”\n• Levels unlock expression only: styles, errand range, titles. The bond screen lists what stays open at any level: the map, replies, friendships, playdates and Whiskers.\n• Most XP comes from approvals and meeting pets. Care is capped at 15 a day. Levels never go down.\n• Missions and the weekly goal never reset a streak. The leaderboard resets every Monday and only ranks real neighbours."
    }
  ],
